  "body": "BitNet b1.58 uses squared ReLU (relu²) in the FFN, but the graph builder was hardcoded to SiLU and the GGUF converters never wrote a `hidden_activation` key.\n\nThis PR makes the activation config-driven:\n\n### llama.cpp submodule changes\n1. **`src/llama-model.cpp`**: Add `\"relu2\"` → `LLM_FFN_RELU_SQR` mapping\n2. **`src/models/bitnet.cpp`**: Read `<arch>.hidden_activation` from GGUF, default to SiLU for backward compat, use `hparams.llm_ffn_op` in graph\n\n### Main repo changes\n3. **`utils/convert-hf-to-gguf-bitnet.py`**: Write `hidden_act(\"relu2\")` for BitNet models\n4. **`utils/convert-ms-to-gguf-bitnet.py`**: Write `hidden_act(\"relu2\")` for BitNet models\n\n### Behavior\n- **New GGUF files** (converted with updated converters): FFN uses ReLU² automatically\n- **Existing GGUF files** (no `hidden_activation` key): FFN uses SiLU (unchanged behavior, no regression)\n\n**Depends on:** https://github.com/isHuangXin/llama.cpp/pull/4\n\nCloses #602",
